<title>ITALY: Italy Senate to vote communications watchdog bill.</title>
<headline>Italy Senate to vote communications watchdog bill.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's Senate (upper house) will vote on Wednesday on a bill setting up a watchdog for the communications sector, parliamentary party leaders said.</p>
<p>The vote was expected by Wednesday evening and followed a decision by the separatist Northern League party on Tuesday to withdraw most of the 3,000-odd amendments it had presented to snarl the bill's progress.</p>
<p>The bill will then pass to the lower Chamber of Deputies.</p>
<p>Establishment of the watchdog body is a prerequisite for privatisation of state telecommunications holding Stet, due to be merged with its operating unit Telecom Italia and sold off later this year.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 2501</p>
